  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government-regulated private law firm. It doesn’t have a binding federal executive order or legal statutes, and its form of government regulation is not seen as binding, except by the courts.\nOfficially known as “The Sheridan Court,” it is the supreme body of judges sitting in one office. In 2017, it steered nearly 2,000 syllabus hours into more than 80 administrative offices.1\nSCOTUS, As Enumerated By the Prime Directive, is A Supreme Court",
